# Debian build profiles used for the DKC kernel build.
#
# One set, version-controlled, passed identically to dependency resolution and
# to the actual build. Passing different sets to the two is how a build ends up
# resolving dependencies it will not use, or using dependencies it did not
# resolve.
#
# Measured against linux 7.1.7-1 on 2026-08-11: this set takes the declared
# amd64 build dependencies from 65 packages to 24.
#
# Each profile is listed with why it is active. Never copy this set to a new
# Debian source revision without re-running: make release-preflight
#
#   nodoc                 Documentation is not part of a DKC deliverable, and it
#                         pulls asciidoctor and the Ruby stack behind it.
#   pkg.linux.notools     perf, cpupower and friends are not DKC packages. This
#                         is the profile that drops most of the closure:
#                         libaudit, libbabeltrace, libdw, libnewt, libnuma,
#                         libopencsd, libperl, libpython3, libtraceevent,
#                         libtracefs, libunwind, python3-dev, python3-docutils,
#                         python3-setuptools, gcc-multilib.
#   pkg.linux.nosource    The linux-source tarball package is not published;
#                         DKC publishes its own complete source package.
#   noudeb                Excludes Debian-installer binary package stanzas.
#   pkg.linux.noudeb      Excludes their architecture build dependencies.
#                         Debian 7.1.7 uses both names, so both are required.
#   pkg.linux.nokerneldbg Debian's kernel debug binary package is not a DKC
#                         deliverable. This does not disable build-time debug
#                         information or BTF; nokerneldbginfo would do that.
#
# Deliberately NOT set:
#
#   pkg.linux.norust      Rust is enabled in Debian's amd64 configuration.
#                         Disabling it to simplify the build is forbidden.
#   pkg.linux.nokerneldbginfo
#                         Disables debug information and BTF, so it is never an
#                         acceptable disk-space optimization for DKC.
#   pkg.linux.mintools    Overlaps with notools; one mechanism is enough.
#
DKC_BUILD_PROFILES="nodoc noudeb pkg.linux.notools pkg.linux.nosource pkg.linux.noudeb pkg.linux.nokerneldbg"
